<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Caracol</h1><p class="st-meta">331 CE – 900 CE (approx.) · capital Caracol</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A major Classic Maya kingdom in the Maya Mountains of Belize, which defeated Tikal in 562 and grew into a sprawling garden city linked by causeways.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Caracol, anciently Oxwitza', was settled by about 600 BCE on a plateau in western <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/belize">Belize</a>. Its royal dynasty is counted from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/te-kab-chaak">Te' K'ab Chaak</a>, who took the throne in 331 CE, and the city grew steadily through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/early-classic-period">Early Classic</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Allied with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kaan">Kingdom of Kaan</a>, Caracol under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yajaw-te-kinich-ii">Yajaw Te' K'inich II</a> defeated <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tikal">Tikal</a> in 562, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kan-ii">K'an II</a> later fought <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/naranjo">Naranjo</a>, recording his victories on monuments including a hieroglyphic stairway found at Naranjo. The city spread over some 200 square kilometres of agricultural terraces and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reservoir">reservoirs</a>, with causeways radiating from the centre and a population that may have exceeded 100,000.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Building continued later than at many lowland cities, with a last dated monument in 859, but Caracol was abandoned by about 900 CE. Excavations since 1985 have made it a key case for understanding Maya urbanism.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/caracol.jpg" alt="Caracol" width="320" height="157"><figcaption>Image: Pgbk87 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panorama_atop_Caracol.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>331 CE – 900 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Caracol</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Yajaw Te' K'inich II, K'an II, K'inich Joy K'awiil</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Maya religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Classic Maya</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/belize">Belize</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Oxwitza', Uxwitza</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=616&amp;focus=caracol" aria-label="Caracol on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2255 1555 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Caracol lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2575 1811L2573 1797"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2573 1797h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2575 1811h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2575 1811h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=616&amp;focus=caracol">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

